{"step_index":5705,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T10:56:22Z","thinking":"Identified the journal blocks associated with Inode 14027084. Proceeding to parse the extents of this inode within the journal data. The file content will be retrieved by reading the physical block from the specified device. The ext4 extent header format `0xF30A` will be used for parsing.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport struct\\n\\nwith open('/tmp/journal.copy', 'rb') as f:\\n    journal = f.read()\\n\\nBLOCK_SIZE = 4096\\n\\n# Check Journal Block 254247 or other blocks\\n# Let's inspect all candidate blocks for 14027084\\nfound = []\\nfor b_idx in [254247, 254248, 254249, 254250, 254253, 254260, 254261, 254276, 254277, 254281, 254283, 254284]:\\n    block = journal[b_idx*BLOCK_SIZE : (b_idx+1)*BLOCK_SIZE]\\n    raw = block[2816 : 2816 + 256]\\n    mode, uid, size = struct.unpack('<HHI', raw[:8])\\n    ext_hdr = raw[40:52]\\n    magic, entries, max_ent, depth, gen = struct.unpack('<HHHHI', ext_hdr)\\n    if magic == 0xF30A and depth == 0 and entries > 0:\\n        # leaf extent\\n        extents = []\\n        for i in range(entries):\\n            off = 52 + i * 12\\n            ee_block, ee_len, ee_start_hi, ee_start_lo = struct.unpack('<IHHI', raw[off:off+12])\\n            pblk = (ee_start_hi << 32) | ee_start_lo\\n            extents.append((ee_block, ee_len, pblk))\\n        found.append((b_idx, size, extents))\\n\\nprint(f'Found {len(found)} valid extent headers for 14027084:')\\nfor b_idx, sz, exts in found:\\n    print(f'   Block {b_idx}: size={sz}, extents={exts}')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Parsing extents for 14027084\"","toolSummary":"\"Parse extents for 14027084\""}}]}
