{"step_index":5707,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T10:56:27Z","thinking":"Different sizes for consecutive blocks suggest a misunderstanding of how the journal works. The block offset within a journal entry doesn't directly translate to a specific filesystem block.\n\nTo determine the corresponding filesystem block, the JBD2 descriptor block must be examined. Understanding the descriptor block's structure is critical.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport struct\\n\\nwith open('/tmp/journal.copy', 'rb') as f:\\n    sb = f.read(4096)\\n\\nmagic, blocktype, seq = struct.unpack('>III', sb[:12])\\nblocksize, maxlen, first, start, sequence = struct.unpack('>IIIII', sb[12:32])\\nprint(f'Journal Superblock:')\\nprint(f'   Magic: {hex(magic)}, blocktype: {blocktype}')\\nprint(f'   Blocksize: {blocksize}, maxlen: {maxlen}, first: {first}, start: {start}, sequence: {sequence}')\\n\\n# Features at offset 0x30 (48)\\ncompat, incompat, ro_compat = struct.unpack('>III', sb[48:60])\\nprint(f'   compat: {bin(compat)}, incompat: {bin(incompat)} (hex: {hex(incompat)}), ro_compat: {bin(ro_compat)}')\\n# JBD2_FEATURE_INCOMPAT_CSUM_V3 = 0x00000010\\n# JBD2_FEATURE_INCOMPAT_64BIT = 0x00000002\\n# JBD2_FEATURE_INCOMPAT_CSUM_V2 = 0x00000008\\nprint(f'   64BIT flag: {bool(incompat & 2)}')\\nprint(f'   CSUM_V2 flag: {bool(incompat & 8)}')\\nprint(f'   CSUM_V3 flag: {bool(incompat & 16)}')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Inspecting journal superblock\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect journal superblock\""}}]}
